Check that we never have duplicate allocations without releasing: we allocate then execute before next allocate.

Check that we never have candidate_dispatch_slot_linked true when we try to allocate again (precondition requires not dispatch_allocated). After allocate, dispatch_allocated becomes true; after execute, we don't have an action that clears dispatch_allocated; but execute_schedule_dispatch effect includes (dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot) but does not affect dispatch_allocated or candidate_dispatch_slot_linked. Actually execute_schedule_dispatch effect: (dispatched ?candidate) (vehicle_available ?vehicle_unit) (dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot). It does not retract dispatch_allocated or candidate_dispatch_slot_linked. So after execute, dispatch_allocated remains true, candidate_dispatch_slot_linked remains true. Then if we try to allocate again for same candidate, precondition not dispatch_allocated would fail. But we allocate only once per candidate, then execute, and we never try to allocate again for same candidate. Good.

For origin and destination, we allocate then execute; we don't reallocate.

Thus plan seems valid.

Now we need to ensure we didn't miss any precondition like candidate_prepared for assign_operator_resource etc. We have that.

Check assign_operator_resource precondition: candidate_prepared and operator_available. We have candidate_prepared after step4/13 etc. Good.

